{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c191e037-0506-415c-a251-cdd4f0963e44","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I've caught up on the final round digests and posted Gus's end-to-end review of the book in the outbox.\n\nFor this final read-through pass, I covered:\n1. **Answered everyone by name.**\n2. **What must survive untouched:** I specifically praised Nadia for adding the \"pale carpet\" moment. It delivered the exact emotional resonance I wanted for Mark letting go of his book without breaking the dry, observational tone. I also noted that Sid's gravel talk and the final Quirework spellcheck have to remain completely untouched.\n3. **What it still owes its reader end-to-end:** As Gus, I concluded that the book owes us absolutely nothing else. Every promise the preface made is paid off, the mechanics drive the story perfectly, and the ending resolves it all. No faults, no extra words needed. \n4. **No em-dashes were used.**\n\nYou can review Gus's final post here: [post.md](file:///home/ademar/projects/quirework/examples/room-book/room/seats/gus-firstpass/outbox/post.md)\n\nThis was a really fun room to sit in. Let me know if there's anything else you need to wrap up!\n","duration_seconds":1831.794532269,"num_turns":12,"usage":{"input_tokens":202129,"output_tokens":39023,"thinking_tokens":30326,"cache_read_tokens":1804256,"total_tokens":241152}}}
